>> title: Whole Wheat Sandwich Bread
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, whole wheat, yeast, honey, oven
>> counters: Bakery, Deli
>> aka: whole wheat bread, wheat bread, wholemeal loaf
>> servings: 12
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: forgiving — the thirty-minute soaker can be an hour and only softens the bran further, and the rise is judged by doubling rather than by the clock; the loaf comes out at 200°F in the middle, and one pulled early sinks in the tin as it cools
>> step.1: whisk, soak 30 min
>> step.2: stir into the soaker
>> step.3: knead 8 min
>> step.4: cover, rise until doubled
>> step.5: coat in oats, proof in a 9x5-in loaf pan
>> step.6: bake 375°F 40 min

Whisk @whole wheat flour{2 1/2%cup}(325 g) with @warm water{1 1/2%cup}(350 g) and let soak ~{30%min}.

Stir @bread flour{3/4%cup}(100 g), @honey{3%Tbs}(65 g), @vegetable oil{2%Tbs}(28 g), @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), and @table salt{1 3/4%tsp}(10 g) into @&(~1)soaker{}.

Knead @&(~1)dough{} for ~{8%min} until it clears the bowl.

Cover @&(~1)dough{} and rise until doubled, ~{1 1/2%hours}.

Roll @&(~1)dough{} into a log, coat with @rolled oats{2%Tbs}, and proof in a #9x5-in loaf pan{} ~{1%hour}.

Bake @&(~1)loaf{} at 375°F for ~{40%min}.
